@@ -0,0 +1,56 @@
+# Local setup with Docker (Postgres + Redis) and scripts
+
+This project now includes helper scripts so you do **not** need to install Postgres/Redis manually.
+
+## 1) Prerequisites
+- Docker Desktop (or Docker Engine + Compose plugin)
+- Java 21
+- Maven 3.9+
+- `psql` and `pg_isready` client tools installed locally
+
+## 2) Start infra
+```bash
+./scripts/start-infra.sh
+```
+This starts:
+- PostgreSQL on `localhost:5432`
+- Redis on `localhost:6379`
+
+## 3) Create all databases + baseline tables
+```bash
+./scripts/init-databases.sh
+```
+This script will:
+- create role `marketplace/marketplace` (if missing)
+- create all service databases
+- grant privileges
+- apply each service `V1__init_*.sql` migration to create tables/indexes
+
+## 4) Start all Spring Boot services
+```bash
+./scripts/start-services.sh
+```
+- starts all modules via `mvn spring-boot:run`
+- writes logs to `.run-logs/`
+- runs `inventory-service` on port `8094` to avoid clash with `search-service` (`8088`)
+
+## 5) One-command bootstrap
+```bash
+./scripts/bootstrap-local.sh
+```
+This runs infra + db init + service startup in one go.
+
+## 6) Import Postman collection
+Import:
+- `postman/marketplace-microservices.postman_collection.json`
+
+Suggested order:
+1. `Auth / Signup`
+2. `Auth / Login` (auto-saves `token`)
+3. Run gateway-routed APIs under `Core APIs via Gateway`
+4. For non-gateway routes, use `Direct service APIs` requests
+
+## 7) Stop infra
+```bash
+./scripts/stop-infra.sh
+```
